WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.201
-Good evening!
I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:03.369
This is "Late Night."

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:04.537
We're so happy
you're with us tonight,

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:05.738
Now we're gonna get to the news.

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:07.740
Today was Thanksgiving,

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:11.211
so congrats on figuring out
your father-in-law's TV.

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:12.345
[ Laughter ]

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:14.247
"You gotta let
the tubes warm up."

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:15.548
[ Laughter ]

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:17.050
That's right.
Today was Thanksgiving,

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.151
and many of us are back
in our hometowns

00:00:19.151 --> 00:00:20.920
at the same tables
as our relatives

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.623
for the first time in two years.
But despite that,

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:25.859
I'd say we still have
a lot to be thankful for.

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:28.995
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:30.997
CNN published an article
this week titled,

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:32.965
"To avoid COVID,
here are four questions

00:00:32.965 --> 00:00:36.002
to ask family and friends ahead
of Thanksgiving gatherees."

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:37.803
"Gatherings" -- excuse me.
"Gatherees"?

00:00:37.803 --> 00:00:39.939
Are they called "gatherees"
or "gatherings"?

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.674
I know where either one works,
right?

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.576
I'm gonna go with "gatherees."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:47.246
That's the Old English.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.246 --> 00:00:50.183
"Join me at a gatheree!"
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:53.953
"For pickled ham!"

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:58.824
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.824 --> 00:01:00.627
CNN published an article
this week titled,

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:03.329
"To avoid COVID,
here are four questions

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:06.465
to ask family and friends ahead
of Thanksgiving gatherings."

00:01:06.465 --> 00:01:08.368
They are,
"Do you watch Fox News?

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:11.204
Have you watched Fox News?
Will you watch Fox News?"

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:13.005
and, "What do you think
of Fox News?"

00:01:13.005 --> 00:01:14.773
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:14.773 --> 00:01:17.444
I'm wondering
if it's less --

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:18.945
I'm wondering if it's
less effective

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:21.648
to burn them after you
pronounce it "gatherees."

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:23.516
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:24.883
New Jersey transit officials

00:01:24.883 --> 00:01:27.053
added additional buses
and train service today

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:28.854
for the Macy's
Thanksgiving Day Parade.

00:01:28.854 --> 00:01:31.925
Unfortunately, they're running
on the exact same route.

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:33.559
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.559 --> 00:01:37.229
Tomorrow is Black Friday,
and consumers can see prices

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:40.366
as low as whatever the full
price was four weeks ago.

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:41.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.503
Inflation comedy!

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:45.438
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.840
Actor Matthew McConaughey
discussed his possible campaign

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.575
for governor of Texas
in a new interview

00:01:49.575 --> 00:01:51.710
with "The Hollywood Reporter,"
which is smart because

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:53.980
Texans famously
get all their news

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:56.916
from "The Hollywood Reporter."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:58.684
Rolls-Royce claimed last week

00:01:58.684 --> 00:02:00.720
that its so-called
Spirit of Innovation plane

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.356
is the fastest
all-electric aircraft

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:06.526
in the world, reaching speeds of
over 345 miles per hour,

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:08.595
which is good
because it's already delayed

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:10.096
two hours out of LaGuardia.

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:12.765
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:14.600
And, finally,
the fast-food chain Popeyes

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:17.236
released its first-ever
vegan option at its new

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:19.639
London location,
which is a Creole

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:21.874
vegan red bean patty burger.

00:02:21.874 --> 00:02:23.976
Because if there's one
thing the English love,

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:26.179
it's putting beans
where they don't belong.

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:28.147
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.147 --> 00:02:31.417
"Come to my breakfast gatheree!"

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:33.586
That was a monologue, everybody!

